{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 55, :comments ["<b>The garment is to be washed.</b> The verb name is not called by the verb form of the heavy added binyan." "<b>It is bald.</b> It has no sibling in Scripture, and it is known in the language of the Rabbis. Its meaning is a deficiency that occurred in the garment's bare spot or in its raised spot. The Gaon [Saadia] said that it was interpreted as the bare spot of the other side, for the raised spot is on the face side of the garment; if so, it would be bare at the back of the head. And he explained well."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:57.736491296Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}